            "description": "Watch Panama vs Croatia highlights and goals from World Cup 2026 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 25, 2026. On June 25, 2026 , the World Cup stage was set for a compelling encounter between Panama and Croatia . Both nations entered the fray seeking crucial points in a match that demanded tactical discipline and clinical finishing. A Cautious Opening Exchange The contest began with Croatia looking to establish their trademark passing rhythm. As early as the 2nd minute, Luka Modric found himself in a scoring position, but his header from a Marco Pasalic cross drifted wide of the target. Panama remained compact and disciplined, offering a threat on the break as Amir Murillo saw a goal-bound effort blocked by the resilient Croatian defense. As the first half progressed, chances remained at a premium. Croatia dominated possession but struggled to find the final ball to penetrate the Panamanian low block. Just before the interval, Martin Baturina nearly broke the deadlock with a right-footed strike from the edge of the area following an Ivan Perisic setup, but the ball whistled past the post, leaving the game scoreless at halftime. Substitutes Direct the Destiny The second half saw Croatia introduce Ante Budimir and Andrej Kramaric in an attempt to spark their offense. The move paid immediate dividends in the 54th minute. Josip Stanisic delivered a pinpoint cross into the six-yard box, and Ante Budimir was perfectly positioned to slot a left-footed finish into the bottom corner, giving his side a vital lead. Panama refused to surrender and mounted a spirited comeback attempt. José Fajardo and Carlos Harvey both went close with headers, while Amir Murillo forced a superb save from Dominik Livakovic in the 68th minute. Despite a flurry of substitutions and a late direct free kick from Murillo that sailed over the bar in stoppage time, Croatia held firm to secure a hard-fought 1-0 victory."
